                <!-- Kick Defender -->
                <div class="getting-started" id="kick-defender">
                    <h2>
                        <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"/></svg>
                        Kick Defender
                    </h2>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">The Kick Defender is a shared-banlist defense network for Kick channels. Log in at <a href="/kick" style="color: var(--accent-green);">certifriedmultitool.com/kick</a> with your Kick account and your channel is protected from the moment you connect &mdash; bad actors and known scam links are removed across every connected channel. You can toggle protection on or off per channel anytime.</p>

                    <h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem;">Getting started</h3>
                    <ol style="color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.7;">
                        <li>Go to <a href="/kick" style="color: var(--accent-green);">/kick</a> and log in with Kick.</li>
                        <li>Your channel is registered and the defender is turned on automatically.</li>
                        <li>If prompted, re-authorize to grant ban + message-management permissions.</li>
                    </ol>

                    <h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem;">Per-channel protection settings</h3>
                    <ul style="color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.7;">
                        <li><strong>Ban type</strong> &mdash; permanent (default) or a timed ban in minutes.</li>
                        <li><strong>Scam-link strikes</strong> &mdash; how many known-scam links a user may post before being banned (default 2; first strike deletes + warns).</li>
                        <li><strong>Custom warning</strong> &mdash; the message shown when a scam link is removed; use <code>{{username}}</code> for a mention.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem;">Manager console</h3>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Managers (assigned by the owner) manage the shared lists at <a href="/kick/managers" style="color: var(--accent-green);">/kick/managers</a>: the banlist, the sublist (fast raid/bot defense), the unban / protection list (whitelist that is never actioned), and manual scam-domain entries. A live lookup checks any domain against the blocklist.</p>

                    <h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem;">Owner admin</h3>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">The owner sees every connected account, its channels, defender status and granted permissions at <a href="/kick/admin" style="color: var(--accent-green);">/kick/admin</a>, and assigns managers from the manager console.</p>

                    <h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem;">Chat commands</h3>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">In Kick chat: <code>!kbd-info</code> (help), <code>!check-ban &lt;user&gt;</code>, <code>!ping</code>. Managers also have <code>!add-ban</code>, <code>!remove-ban</code>, <code>!add-sublist</code>, <code>!add-unban</code>, <code>!mod-check</code>.</p>
                </div>

